    "description": "The Pyramid is easily viewable from the decks of Kokanee Glacier Cabin by looking Southwest. It's found a few hundred metres down the North ridge of Mount Kitchener and looks like a pyramid from a distance. The Nothwest face offers some good skiing very close to the cabin however the upper routes are often wind scoured by prevailing winds coming North from Kokanee Lake Pass.",
    "source": "backcountryskiingcanada.com (via guide PDF)"
