      "description": "Knee D-2 is a route that starts just below the Pyramid and leads directly into J.C's to provide a much longer ski descent than the previous two routes mentioned. To access Knee D-2 again climb Southeast up Smuggler's Ridge, this time skin higher up to 2,400 metres just below The Pyramid. Caution is required as the terrain is open and gradually gets steeper as you skin higher. Ski down with caution eventually reaching the start of J.C.'s and continue skiing amongst the sparse trees avoiding any steeper sections and cliff bands. At the bottom of the valley you will only be a short distance to Keen Lake and from here it's a short, flat skin back to Kaslo Lake and Kokanee Glacier Cabin.",
